Addresses 11 review comments from PR#216 (latency optimization) covering parameter inconsistencies, type safety, race conditions, and dead code.

## Backend (Python)
- **orchestrator_core.py**: Removed unused `context` parameter causing signature confusion
- **llm_simple.py**: Added `max_length=50000` validation to `SimpleChatRequest.content`

## Frontend (TypeScript/React)
- **chat-mode-routing.spec.ts**: Added `Page` type annotation to test helper
- **cockpit-home.tsx**: 
  - Fixed history deduplication to keep latest entry by timestamp using Date comparison
  - Handles null/undefined timestamps properly
  - Removed dead code (`userEntryAdded` flag)
- **conversation-bubble.tsx**: Optimized typing effect with `requestAnimationFrame`, added bounds check
- **use-task-stream.ts**: Fixed SSE/polling race condition by checking `source.readyState` before polling

## Developer Experience
- **package.json**: Split monolithic `test:e2e` into `test:e2e:latency` and `test:e2e:functional`
- **playwright.config.ts**: Clarified Next.js API proxy comment

Example of deduplication fix:

```typescript
// Before: string comparison, no null handling
if (!existing || (entry.timestamp && existing.timestamp && entry.timestamp > existing.timestamp)) {
  seenMap.set(key, entry);
}

// After: Date comparison, explicit null handling
if (!existing) {
  seenMap.set(key, entry);
} else if (entry.timestamp && existing.timestamp) {
  if (new Date(entry.timestamp) > new Date(existing.timestamp)) {
    seenMap.set(key, entry);
  }
} else if (entry.timestamp && !existing.timestamp) {
  seenMap.set(key, entry);
}
```

